**Omitted: `execution`** — it has no deliverables, artifacts, assets, commits or sessions in the window, no first/last activity, and its missions are all closed or stopped. Its stored resume line is just the thread's own name. There was nothing to read honestly, so it gets no synthesis rather than an invented one.

`why` blocks are keyed to index `"0"` only for the threads whose records actually generate a decision item — the ones with an unfinished line (`extract-forge`, `01-listing-content`, `video-studio-edit-bay`) or enough idle time to trigger the resume-or-park item (`system-audit`, `go`). The rest get no `why`.

The read that came out of the bundle, since it's the same shape across almost every thread: **the system's build capacity isn't the constraint, deployment is.** The listening engine runs but scores under the bar every time. The video studio renders but has only ever seen a test clip. The character assets are fully built and have never appeared in public. The extraction forge is done and its output is logged as usage-tracked, not revenue-bearing. One thread — the LinkedIn campaign — has daily motion, and even there every record is production, none is response.

